h you can shape and i find it  really exciting it's actually one of my  favorite parts of making a film  did you actually make any big changes in  the editing room that you weren't  expecting  um big changes no  we like there's scenes where we cut  dialogue so like maybe now they only say  three or four lines but originally in  the script there were ten lines um  there's a few little scenes that were  cut entirely from the movie but nothing  they weren't like important they were  kind of just little moments um so and i  think that's fairly normal so no i would  say we didn't make any large changes at  all  uh  jonathan and lily i i'm curious uh what  is it like actually watching  your work and lily especially for you  because you this is your first movie  what what is it actually like watching  it for the first time and can you sort  of take yourself like are you very  self-conscious or can you  you know what i mean yeah  so i was absolutely terrified to watch  it for the first time um i was trying to  think of ways out of it in fact but i  knew it was too important and i was too  invested in the story itself to  skip that um  as soon as i pressed play  i was able to set aside any kind of  insecurities or  you know fixations on my appearance or  my voice all of those things that would  necessarily kind of cringe you out about  yourself on tape and just try to  fall into the narrative as much as i  could so that i could really enjoy the  work that everybody poured into this  right on right down to the pas it felt  like such a kind of family effort so i'm  proud of myself for being able to put my  insecurities aside and and just sort of  enjoy  um or  be moved by the story  i i i'm proud of myself for the way i  coped in the end  i'm not sure i'm going to be re-watching  it necessarily but  um i think you know what what happens on  the set of a confident um artist like  jamie is that your everybody is has  prepared all of their work and then they  come on the day and 